text:
A BANKER:
(to himself.)
I never knew any year worse for money upon interest, than this year has turned out to me. From morning even until night, I spend my time in the Forum;

A BANKER:
(apart.)
He’s coming towards me. I’m all right I’ve some hopes of my money;

A BANKER:
(to THEUROPIDES.)
Really, don’t think much of that;

TRANIO:
(to himself, as he goes to the other side of the stage to call THEUROPIDES.)
They say that Alexander the Great and Agathocles achieved two very great exploits; what shall be the lot of myself, a third, who, unaided, am achieving deeds imperishable? This old fellow is carrying his pack-saddle, the other one, as well. I’ve hit upon a novel trade for myself, not a bad one;
